{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.KernelGrowthBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.KernelGrowthBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ow_const_on_rescales","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ow_const_on_rescales","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/KernelGrowthBound.lean#L174-L185","doc":"If a grading is invariant under rescaling by non-zero reals, then every\nrescaling of an element shares its grade: `ordω` sees the growth class, never\nthe constant.\n\nThis is `OmegaOrder.Ow_ofReal_mul` stated without the surreal-field scaffolding,\nand it is the same phenomenon `SurrealGradingPrune` proves is *forced* rather\nthan assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.bounded_of_kernel_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.bounded_of_kernel_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/KernelGrowthBound.lean#L154-L165","doc":"**Sub-geometric kernels give bounded solutions.** If the kernel's `ℓ¹` norm\nis at most `1`, no solution can grow at all — the bound is uniform in `n`.\n\nThe contrapositive is the useful direction for an obstruction argument: an\n*unbounded* solution certifies `|a₀| + |a₁| > 1`, a purely algebraic conclusion\ndrawn from archimedean data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.growth_bound_depth2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.growth_bound_depth2","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/KernelGrowthBound.lean#L104-L152","doc":"**Growth bound from the kernel alone.**\n\nFor any solution of the depth-2 recurrence `B(n+2) = a₁·B(n+1) + a₀·B(n)`, if\nthe initial window is bounded by `C` and `R ≥ 1` dominates the kernel's `ℓ¹`\nnorm `|a₀| + |a₁|`, then `|B n| ≤ C·Rⁿ` for every `n`.\n\nThe growth exponent is read off the **coefficients**; nothing about the\nsolution's analytic behaviour is used. This is the depth-2 case of\n`prop:binding-genfun-qdifference`(1): the scale rule is an output of the\nkernel, not a fitted constant. ","signatureChunk":0}]}